[Chapter 25] [Psalm of Supplication] “To You, O LORD, I lift up my soul”
It is a psalm of repentance and supplication, in acrostic form (each line begins with the first letter or first word following the order of the Hebrew alphabet), in which, trusting in the lovingkindness of God even amid tribulation, one confesses sin and asks for forgiveness.
[Psalms 25:1] [Of David.] To You, O LORD, I lift up my soul;

[Chapter 36] The word concerning the restoration of Israel
It prophesies that the devastated land of Israel will be restored and become fruitful, and that the people of Israel will also be restored.
In chapter 34, God promises to give a new leader (shepherd) who will guide Israel into a land of peace and life;
in chapter 35, He declares the destruction of the people of Edom, who were defiling the land of Canaan where the people of Judah had lived;
and in chapter 36, as a more concrete promise of restoration, He presents the promise of the restoration of the land where they will dwell.
